# Copy to .env (or .env.production) and adjust. Vite inlines these at BUILD
# time, not runtime — a change here needs a rebuild, and anything defined here
# ships to the browser, so never put a secret in this file.

# Origin the backend API is served from.
#
# Leave empty for local development: `npm run dev` proxies /api to
# http://localhost:8000 (see vite.config.ts), and an empty base keeps every
# request a same-origin relative path. The same is true in production when the
# SPA and the API sit behind one reverse proxy on the same origin.
#
# Set this only when the SPA is served from a different origin than the API
# (e.g. the SPA on static hosting, the API on its own host). Note that
# `vite preview` does NOT apply the dev proxy, so previewing a production
# build against a local backend needs an explicit value here.
#
# No trailing slash required — one is stripped automatically.
# Example: VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.framegrader.example.com
#
# Whatever origin the SPA is served from must also be listed in the backend's
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS, or the browser will block the request at CORS.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
